#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198053 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ea202ce3-07d4-5324-9ee4-f5617b430772" :question/math-academy-id "e-12477" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R,$ defined as\n\n![](images/55/55831f05bb13347baf6816e77b462b893906cead512607cc4caf796440bbc2d7.svg)\n\ncalculate $\\boldsymbol f'$ at ![](images/ab/abac407b29e870cfe7090d3a263109f10a122fe1de14abbd76baef6d7101b3d2.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/28/286bec34ba72c733264e8223150d56566d0f61797cb221bed0af0323c3e190c9.svg) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol f$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol f$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/33/33b42ebfc6c3f32ef92212f61a138080543e2e2981088f7b5760b23f7ac31c6c.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/35/354f034a96ffe5bde885644792f50636dc8cbde6f00d65159b0bdefdd836fa09.svg)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)=2xy, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/90/900488a105afb5aa10e9113db36cd9f2e834eac46300d7c0a521a7100ae0d88f.svg)\n\nand $\\boldsymbol{f}'$ at ![](images/ed/ed7c974c8fca89e98f542231572e558caf867b200843d2b222ccda4c68a1c33b.svg) is\n\n![](images/ab/abd152888f711ecd43a47e31269e40985178782591546e9d96912fd4c230afa0.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198054 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198412 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "ea76d21f-eff8-5634-975f-2b5bd24caf54" :question/math-academy-id "e-12478" :question/problem "For the transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R^3,$ defined as\n\n![](images/bb/bbb9192192b4d73f4993b3131a2b0bb1d0a0cddb77b754940d1b7684bfb08336.svg)\n\nthe total derivative $\\boldsymbol f'$ is given by \n\n![](images/2c/2cf231879630af578e33b201e5be0f65d019da9c49da7789f5921c05a8249c09.svg)\nFrom top to bottom, what are the missing entries?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/49/49c118b037a1589c6feb2c96afeaccb15fe905663393800638baff8cef327a3a.svg) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/a5/a5ed3766e8ed6a2a5fd249078e244dfab19b1c20d55548c27a7053bd0130c278.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/23/23d7804912a10685756bb4ec89d12e3f6659b435ebe4d22c436684fb6eef9df8.svg)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=x, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})=2y, \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{y}{x},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/ea/eae5dd91db0cc17bec3af0a4781c7a58e8c65edb6c4139642f9c806dfc9c2473.svg)\nThus, the missing entries are $y,\\:$ $0,\\:$ and $\\ln{x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198055 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198413 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "db0be438-94fe-52de-9daf-60d1727ce7b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12479" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R,$ defined as\n\n![](images/7c/7c033fac25d53675fc47eaf5184d33f95c6e3524d82a4c547fb900e13c5205f7.svg)\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at ![](images/9c/9c89326030e3216291d4c0fbd715cdd634a567b6dae3f0d26620d19ee5f470ea.svg) is given by\n\n![](images/62/62ad44fc4734bc7006e9cc72a3e142d2df1d932f3fcdf1c0c6c125e8bd19d626.svg)\n\nfind the missing values." :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/82/826e5972b8b35e46f759dfb8f465316db48e36b12ef37d73b7bce6931f65a3d9.svg) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/85/85c62ebacb5d1aaf052165a76d44b42dc83a2918020320326fd4bbe8cc4da14c.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/93/93faf7b5ccbadf7600ec47c7e63cac088211130f0f30109fbc71f2d7081139b9.svg)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})=3{x}^{2},\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})={e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/65/65e55a996288ffb34ef5b44b9b49dc7adaf681d379625733e7e74f8363f3f36f.svg)\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at ![](images/6a/6a0a72041eadc608c5f2ef7217a5e627115cee3bce332751a5cb46acd9dc0c24.svg) we have\n\n![](images/ee/ee17f93ff906242db59f3ef934b9501e7335a46ba5710e3fd89645e83be5ba34.svg)\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - f(\\mathbf a) = \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(\\mathbf a),$ $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a),$ and $\\mathbf a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n![](images/42/42b3574762b1d9b14d27f8ba29b5c89bca66ec03724fbec7557c7bf6e5524972.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198056 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198414 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f3540571-9159-50b4-a46c-4cf28a454602" :question/math-academy-id "e-12484" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^2\\to\\mathbb R^2,$ defined as\n\n![](images/f8/f8eb8b775c1645d73acd7313f54bdff4cdb55830ac6ebea2165c9263321ffb9e.svg)\n\nIf the linear approximation of $\\boldsymbol f$ at ![](images/18/18b82def6f36d90157e99ef72f14b857cd1e0c3007e684c660c31fd61f805040.svg) is given by\n\n![](images/91/91e5867a6be8302649edc9c2e1e4c4642c60853c7c3ad9bb2d25f9c649b5889d.svg)\n\nwhat are the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $\\boldsymbol{f}:\\mathbb R^n\\to\\mathbb R^m$ is defined by \n\n![](images/43/43ffd01ab7a6d78ea0343953b985d9c4165ee76085f345bcd500c053550e3ec9.svg) \n\nwhere $f_1,f_2,\\ldots,f_m$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $\\boldsymbol{f}$ is differentiable at $\\mathbf{x},$ then the total derivative of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf{x},$ denoted $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf{x}),$ is given by the $m \\times n$ matrix\n\n![](images/51/51191f4e8b1417de7b391a71d68c7c5917ed7083cc3b7a630662d6a0912b969c.svg)\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n![](images/06/066be34bb8bd7f585bc3d2666007e189f6c82f2e3b7f7a699928066825fd765d.svg)\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1})={x}_{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{1},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{2})=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n![](images/86/869b2f5de537961c4c83523ac6fcfd96329fc062e34509d88b8516b7a2259b84.svg)\n\nEvaluating $\\boldsymbol{f}$ and its derivative at ![](images/b3/b35d7585ed24aea694c3a31e69c1406744986db30cddf8842a5bae8d6d745e4b.svg) we have\n\n![](images/9f/9f3dbb19be577a74b8f19fd1eb5d42910fd0e46637388a3daab80c17d6edd833.svg)\n\nThe linear approximation of $\\boldsymbol{f}$ at $\\mathbf x = \\mathbf a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}\\left(\\mathbf x \\right) \\approx \\boldsymbol{f}(\\mathbf a) + \\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a)(\\mathbf x - \\mathbf a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\boldsymbol{f}(\\mathbf a),$ $\\boldsymbol{f}'(\\mathbf a),$ and $\\mathbf a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n![](images/5d/5d526b2485b53b029bc119e66e6a385d0ba228ecca1ffd0c58e7934e83a97a7b.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198412 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a818e04-786a-56b6-90cf-dcb573ccfa64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52ae776e-08b3-54b7-a885-e9217261d1b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}y,\\,$ $\\frac{1}{z},\\,$ and ${x}^{2}y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427508} {:answer/id #uuid "595978fe-cf25-5127-9b94-47cb53657dd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}y,\\,$ $\\frac{1}{x},\\,$ and ${x}^{2}y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427509} {:answer/id #uuid "b28b947e-e099-5a84-a1f1-e49c76339f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2xyz,\\,$ $\\frac{1}{y},\\,$ and $yz$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427513} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8a1cde-3900-5ec2-8cba-bd78da711720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2xyz,\\,$ $\\frac{1}{z},\\,$ and ${y}^{2}z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427514} {:answer/id #uuid "f3204833-987c-5155-a299-7bcc45208ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2xyz,\\,$ $\\frac{1}{y},\\,$ and ${x}^{2}y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3204833-987c-5155-a299-7bcc45208ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2xyz,\\,$ $\\frac{1}{y},\\,$ and ${x}^{2}y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427516} :answer-field/id #uuid "d21567a5-5f65-5300-b094-9bc5b4d4fdfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8b4c68b-51c3-543e-a36a-3adc1afaee33" :question/math-academy-id "q-162942" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz) \\\\ {x}^{2}yz\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${f}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{x} & \\bbox[3pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} & \\frac{1}{z} \\\\ \\bbox[3pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}} & {x}^{2}z & \\bbox[3pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing entries?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))=\\frac{1}{x},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))=\\frac{1}{y},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))=\\frac{1}{z} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}yz)=2xyz,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}yz)={x}^{2}z,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}yz)={x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{x} & \\frac{1}{y} & \\frac{1}{z} \\\\ 2xyz & {x}^{2}z & {x}^{2}y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e5bacbe-aa5e-5d50-a8d3-828530f6f794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509786} {:answer/id #uuid "a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510031} {:answer/id #uuid "e2146baa-0d3c-5c31-b8af-6a549c415146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ 2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510169} {:answer/id #uuid "e90042bd-8e4a-560f-9816-a073ad2b6499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2x\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510189} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc39ef3-38f5-5f8a-b8a6-a4db0fe5e8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a45c6d66-2d06-51e5-a78c-7919e520c702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510031} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ebf2c22-6a63-56b3-856c-34ea1cbbe684" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71f7e517-e1ae-5c37-961e-c4ca36d1869e" :question/math-academy-id "q-162943" :question/problem "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 2y\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198414 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f09fc28-bdce-554f-98f5-019d34542a13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Affine Approximation of a Vector Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f469356-0c49-54f5-97c7-81d3ca327f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279151} {:answer/id #uuid "4b5f92ac-fc92-5f32-8c13-fc44705bd983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279266} {:answer/id #uuid "c5cd7907-3281-5924-a02d-4944e88430a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280328} {:answer/id #uuid "e07f4e0d-b768-563e-8a76-0b93ddad1910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280576} {:answer/id #uuid "e7fa5133-a430-53a4-b9d6-a94204dbb514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5cd7907-3281-5924-a02d-4944e88430a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280328} :answer-field/id #uuid "f40528cb-fde2-5a1d-88ab-741000eebbb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8bf8960-3077-5130-9de0-3e5c9b2bef5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-162944" :question/problem "Consider the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf the linear approximation of $f$ at $a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix}$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈\\begin{bmatrix}∗ \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 2\\end{bmatrix}(x-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix}),\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})=2{x}_{2},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{1}{x}_{2})=2{x}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}})={x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}})={x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} & 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}} & {x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}{x}_{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{f}^{′}(a)=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}(x-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198413 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e90349c-33ae-5b60-9d0d-7542dfebbbc7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent Plane to the Graph of a Scalar Function in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abf05005-bb55-52ea-bdeb-0af8bce6ebf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194448} {:answer/id #uuid "e176522b-f194-5621-b102-9a1f8172e9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194449} {:answer/id #uuid "ef015efb-b40c-5213-8013-ea9116552ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194450} {:answer/id #uuid "fad445fa-9a23-5167-a2a6-ab4823d562be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194451} {:answer/id #uuid "08e943aa-8f6f-517a-a862-2eeb69b815cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e176522b-f194-5621-b102-9a1f8172e9f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194449} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0df6f8b-e886-541d-a0b0-bbd34e003cb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94a03db3-689e-5f9f-9952-8aa2d787372b" :question/math-academy-id "q-162945" :question/problem "Consider the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}+y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf the tangent to $f$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-∗=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}])\n$$\n\nwhat is the sum of the missing values?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)=2x,\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=0,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-0=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+2+1=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198642 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64bfb38d-b820-561c-bd14-251aa2edcfd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509897} {:answer/id #uuid "d56da6ba-7a81-51ff-9ea5-12ef733832ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510139} {:answer/id #uuid "ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510201} {:answer/id #uuid "f01f7bc7-3557-591c-9f22-1bdedc02c03b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510203} {:answer/id #uuid "fd35a67f-7792-58f7-89e6-7cec7aeef019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee29d73a-7b18-567a-8d48-75d2695369be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510201} :answer-field/id #uuid "e32a9a36-798d-559e-9317-93926f5a547f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35c044c4-8c10-5b2a-9efa-fdd94802179a" :question/math-academy-id "q-162983" :question/problem "For the transformation $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={x}^{2}-2y,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2y)=2x, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nand ${f}^{′}$ at $a=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}2(0) & -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "837de383-8a59-5e3e-b44b-4a83acba37f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389390} {:answer/id #uuid "1476b37b-ce46-5ab0-aecb-36dc6b67bf4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389391} {:answer/id #uuid "9267d816-5255-57ea-9f4e-ac44e66b36b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389392} {:answer/id #uuid "cb2c5eb2-ed70-5a83-8ae7-1ccc3e1b1655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389393} {:answer/id #uuid "c6dfc81d-0308-5b8f-a138-4ee9b7abef58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb2c5eb2-ed70-5a83-8ae7-1ccc3e1b1655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389393} :answer-field/id #uuid "1904f0bd-e59f-53c2-902e-e5c624a33494" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "481039ec-e171-5d00-9cb6-0349111018af" :question/math-academy-id "q-163033" :question/problem "For the function $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\ncalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & \\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d912b296-6fd0-57c2-84e8-ca0b56549756" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Scalar Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43e47057-a760-57db-a3bf-60ce0300791b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y{e}^{xy} & x{e}^{xy}\\end{bmatri